== Simulation: first worker start 5s slower
-- old tests (81133d3), whole file:
E       AssertionError: assert ('UNKNOWN' == 'WORLD_UNVERIFIED'
E         + UNKNOWN)
FAILED tests/unit/test_zz_coldsim_old_budget.py::test_one_budget_covers_the_whole_compiled_decision
1 failed, 3 passed in 8.06s
-- hardened tests, whole file:
4 passed in 12.67s

The old file ran under a temporary name, tests/unit/test_zz_coldsim_old_budget.py, beside the hardened one.
Cause, as far as these runs show: each inner run's latency limit is a real solver deadline (45% of it),
while the tests' budget clock is fake. A short real deadline does not always hold the first solver start
after a container restore; the cortex then reports UNKNOWN (TIMEOUT), which is the correct result. The
hardened tests give every inner run a real limit of 20s or more (9s or more for the solver) and
keep the same budget logic on the fake clock. The restore-time slowness itself was not measured directly: it was gone by the time
it was looked for (a fresh -I import of ortools and z3 took 0.35s after dropping the page cache).
